message: "If you use this code, data or these results, please cite them as below."
title: "The Hadwiger–Nelson problem over number fields"
abstract: >-
  Exact-arithmetic tools, data and machine-checked certificates for the
  Hadwiger–Nelson problem on the chromatic number of the plane. Includes a
  short proof that the planes over Q(sqrt2, sqrt3) and Q(sqrt3, sqrt11) are
  4-chromatic (the latter a theorem of K. G. Fischer, 1994), with a note and
  formal proofs in Lean 4; OpenAI's proof that chi(R^2) >= 6 checked in Lean
  and run over the constructible (ruler-and-compass) numbers; chi(R^2) <= 7 and
  chi(R^2) in {6, 7} in Lean in the statement of formal-conjectures; four
  colours for the planes over Q(sqrt d), d = 11 (mod 12); results on two and
  three colours over number fields, circular chromatic numbers and p-adic
  planes; reproductions of chi(R^2) >= 4 and >= 5 with DRAT certificates; and
  certified bounds showing that several finite planes need six colours.
  AI-assisted research; not peer reviewed.
